<section class="py-2">
  <h1 class="max-w-3xl text-4xl leading-[1.1] md:text-5xl">When one merchant gets burned, every merchant can <span class="hl-blue">learn from it</span>.</h1>
  <div class="mt-6 grid items-start gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[1.2fr_1fr]">
    <div class="space-y-4 text-lg text-ink-soft">
      <p>OpenTrust is a free, shared notebook where Indian merchants note down <span class="hl">mobile numbers that caused them trouble</span>: chargebacks and disputed payments, fake orders, callers posing as a bank to ask for an OTP, refused cash-on-delivery orders, and the like.</p>
      <p>Before you fulfil an order, check whether another merchant has written something down. It's a community effort, and we're not trying to make money from it.</p>
      <div class="rounded-md border-2 border-teal bg-white p-4 text-base text-ink">
        <p class="text-xl font-extrabold">You don't have to share a single real phone number.</p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-ink-soft">Hash the number on your side and send that instead: we match on the hash and <strong class="text-ink">never receive the number</strong>. One option in our Ruby and Node libraries, or a few lines in any language. <%= link_to "See how", docs_path(anchor: "hashing"), class: "text-blue underline" %></p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-ink-soft">A hash limits what is sent and stored; it can in principle be reversed, so it does not make anyone anonymous.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <p class="text-lg font-extrabold">Set up <span class="hl">for free</span></p>
      <ul class="mt-3 space-y-1 text-sm">
        <li>✓ <%= number_with_delimiter(OpenTrust::FREE_CHECKS) %> free checks once approved</li>
        <li>✓ No card, no sales call</li>
        <li>✓ API key and docs from day one</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="mt-4 grid grid-cols-2 gap-3">
        <%= link_to "Get started", register_path, class: "btn" %>
        <%= link_to "Read the docs", docs_path, class: "btn-quiet" %>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="mt-10" aria-labelledby="intro-video">
  <h2 id="intro-video" class="text-2xl">The problem, in under a minute</h2>
  <button type="button" class="vthumb mt-4" data-action="video#open" aria-haspopup="dialog">
    <img src="/video/opentrust-intro-poster.jpg" alt="" width="1280" height="720" loading="lazy">
    <span class="vthumb-play" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M8 5.5v13l11-6.5z"/></svg></span>
    <span class="vthumb-label data">Play the intro · 0:57</span>
    <span class="sr-only">Play the intro video in a window</span>
  </button>
</section>

<section class="mt-10" data-controller="receipt">
  <div class="tabs">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap" role="tablist">
      <button type="button" role="tab" class="tab" data-receipt-target="tab" data-action="receipt#pick">Number has reports</button>
      <button type="button" role="tab" class="tab" data-receipt-target="tab" data-action="receipt#pick">Nothing reported</button>
    </div>
    <div class="rounded-md bg-white p-5">
      <div class="grid items-center gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
        <div>
          <p class="data text-xs text-ink-soft">POST /api/v1/lookups · 1 check</p>
          <div class="stack mt-3">
          <div data-receipt-target="state" data-active="true">
            <h2 class="text-2xl">See what others have noted</h2>
            <p class="mt-2 text-ink-soft">Two verified merchants noted the same experience with this number. You see what happened and their notes, never who wrote them.</p>
            <p class="tag mt-4 border-amber bg-amber-wash text-ink">Noted by 2 verified merchants</p>
          </div>
          <div data-receipt-target="state" data-active="false">
            <h2 class="text-2xl">An empty list is good news</h2>
            <p class="mt-2 text-ink-soft">No merchant has noted anything about this number. A check costs the same either way.</p>
            <p class="tag mt-4 border-teal text-teal">Nothing reported</p>
          </div>
          </div>
          <p class="mt-4 text-xs text-ink-soft">Reports are unverified observations from individual merchants, not a finding about anyone.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="win data text-sm">
          <div class="win-bar"><span class="win-dot"></span><span class="win-dot"></span><span class="win-dot"></span><span class="ml-2">response.json</span></div>
          <div class="p-4 stack">
            <div data-receipt-target="code" data-active="true">
<pre class="whitespace-pre-wrap break-words">{
  "phone_last4": "3210",
  "reported": <span class="font-bold text-amber">true</span>,
  "report_count": 2,
  "reports": [{
    "reason_code": "<span class="text-amber">chargeback</span>",
    "notes": "Disputed 3 card payments",
    "reporter_verified": true
  }, …],
  "notice": "Unverified observations…"
}</pre>
            </div>
            <div data-receipt-target="code" data-active="false">
<pre class="whitespace-pre-wrap break-words">{
  "phone_last4": "0147",
  "reported": <span class="font-bold text-teal">false</span>,
  "report_count": 0,
  "reports": [],
  "notice": "Unverified observations…"
}</pre>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="how" class="mt-14 grid gap-10 md:grid-cols-2">
  <div>
    <h2 class="text-3xl">Why this is <span class="hl">free</span></h2>
    <div class="mt-3 space-y-3 text-ink-soft">
      <p>We built OpenTrust because fraud quietly drains honest businesses, and through them, India's digital economy. When merchants warn each other, the same bad actor has a harder time moving on to the next store.</p>
      <p>That only works if lots of merchants take part, so we don't charge for it. Every approved merchant gets <strong class="text-ink"><%= number_with_delimiter(OpenTrust::FREE_CHECKS) %> checks</strong>. Run out? Write to us, tell us what you're building, and we'll sort out a generous limit.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div>
    <h2 class="text-3xl">Built to be <span class="hl">careful</span></h2>
    <dl class="mt-3 space-y-4">
      <div><dt class="font-extrabold">You share only the number, or just its hash</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">No customer names, addresses or order data ever reach us, because you never send them. Prefer not to send even the number? Send its SHA-256 hash instead. (A hash limits what is sent and stored; it can in principle be reversed, so it does not make anyone anonymous.)</dd></div>
      <div><dt class="font-extrabold">Reporters stay anonymous</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Other merchants see what happened, the note and a "verified merchant" badge. Never a business name.</dd></div>
      <div><dt class="font-extrabold">Numbers are protected</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Matching uses a keyed hash and the stored copy is encrypted. Lookups return only the last 4 digits.</dd></div>
      <div><dt class="font-extrabold">Mistakes get fixed</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">If something was noted in error, our <%= link_to "grievance process", privacy_path, class: "text-blue underline" %> exists to put it right.</dd></div>
    </dl>
    <%= link_to "Read the FAQ", faq_path, class: "btn-quiet mt-6" %>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="mt-14 border-t border-line pt-10" aria-labelledby="participants">
  <p id="participants" class="text-sm font-bold text-ink-soft">Merchants already on OpenTrust</p>
  <ul class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
    <% OpenTrust::PARTICIPANTS.each do |m| %>
      <li><%= link_to m[:url], target: "_blank", rel: "noopener noreferrer", class: "flex h-16 items-center rounded-lg bg-[#1F2937] px-4 transition hover:opacity-90", title: "#{m[:name]} (opens in a new tab)" do %><%= image_tag m[:logo], alt: m[:name], class: "h-11 w-auto" %><% end %></li>
    <% end %>
    <li><%= link_to "Add your business →", register_path, class: "text-sm font-bold text-blue underline" %></li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="mt-14 rounded-lg border border-line bg-white p-6 md:p-8">
  <h2 class="text-3xl">Help us make India <span class="hl">win</span></h2>
  <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-ink-soft">OpenTrust only works if merchants build it together. Got an idea to make the ecosystem better, a pattern we should cover, or something that's getting in your way? Reach out to us. We read everything.</p>
  <div class="mt-5 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4">
    <%= mail_to OpenTrust::FEEDBACK_EMAIL, OpenTrust::FEEDBACK_EMAIL, class: "btn data" %>
    <% if OpenTrust::COFFEE_URL %>
      <%= link_to "Buy us a coffee ☕", OpenTrust::COFFEE_URL, class: "btn-quiet", rel: "noopener" %>
    <% end %>
  </div>
  <% if OpenTrust::COFFEE_URL %>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-sm text-ink-soft">If OpenTrust helps your business and you'd like to say thanks, a coffee is always welcome. It's never expected, and it never changes what you get.</p>
  <% end %>
</section>
